  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4c7d567a-6834-534b-886b-898fda7a8924" activityNameId="2680ea72-d85c-53ea-8bed-6997cf2492c4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Wind turbine 5MW, offshore, jacket substructure</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Wind turbine 5MW, offshore, jacket substructure
UUID=c1666d68-463b-3134-88fe-f7c22b884153
Wind turbine substructure (including transition piece), at site including manufacturing, transports, installation, replacements, decommission and waste treatement. Calculated for FU of 1p.
Data of material inputs are based on the offshore wind turbine REpower 5M, with a nominal capacity of 5 MW, as used in the Ormonde offshore wind farm, UK.
The modelled substructure represents a jacket foundation including piles, lattice and transition piece.
The distance to installation port is assumed to be 187 km. The average water depth is 19 m. 
Assumed lifetime is 25 years.

Main data source regarding material composition: 
Kouloumpis, V., &amp; Azapagic, A. (2022). A model for estimating life cycle environmental impacts of offshore wind electricity considering specific characteristics of wind farms. Sustainable Production and Consumption, 29, 495–506. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spc.2021.10.024
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c1666d68-463b-3134-88fe-f7c22b884153.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
